A bachelor’s or master’s degree from an accredited college or university in Computer Science,
Information Systems, or other related field, or four (12) years of equivalent work experience is required.
Relevant experience may be substituted for education on a year-for-year basis when applicable.

Skills, and knowledge for this position:
• Possess a Project Management Professional (PMP®) Certification;
• Ten or more years managing successful, large-scale projects with multiple diverse teams;
• Ten or more years of experience in change management methodologies, strategies, and implementation;
• Ten or more years utilizing project management software (e.g., Microsoft Project, Primavera, and/or Jira) to track and maintain projects;
• Ten or more years of experience with project management methodologies and documentation (e.g., PMO);
• Ten or more years of experience in risk and issue management;
• Five (5) or more years of experience facilitating meetings and developing clear documentation;
• Experience creating and presenting status reports to internal and external stakeholders;
• Ability to coordinate project teams, lead complex projects, and meet objectives; Demonstrated leadership and negotiation skills.
• Proficient in communicating clearly with both technical and non-technical stakeholders.

